**Read:** [Polymer-composite weathering protocols — NIST SP 1200-15](../sources/Polymer-Weathering-Protocols-NIST.lingua#r_2WPNZEDVAHNBVD1GS5W878PZCG) and [Outdoor polymer service-life inference — Duan and colleagues](../sources/Polymer-Service-Life-Duan-and-Colleagues.lingua#r_06S8ZC7PTSPQYJJTFMH97NFFTT) in full, with underlying measurement and statistical methods. Use [Spacecraft polymer atomic-oxygen durability — NASA-HDBK-6024](../sources/Atomic-Oxygen-Durability-NASA.lingua#r_1RMMZEYQQCZ08VRYTHCQBEEHJ0) as a deliberately different ground-to-service comparison.

Reconstruct formulation, conditioning, spectrum, temperature, humidity and response measurement for a polymer study. Connect a chemical or morphological signal with a required function. Derive a reaction/transport or dose account, compare alternative acceleration assumptions and independently verify the inference. Distinguish inaccessible proprietary feed details from quantities that were actually measured.

**Deliver:** A reproducible model, depth or specimen-size reasoning, covariance/variability treatment, functional-threshold sensitivity and an outdoor or independently held-out prediction. Explain any missing raw-data limitation without manufacturing observations. Compare laboratory and service damage evidence before interpreting an acceleration factor. Propose and justify a new observation that would separate the principal competing explanations.

